  "main_findings": [
    "Exact target-level evidence burden was monotone under both ecological-world expansion and assay-observation-world expansion, with zero violations across all 387 fiber-transformation rows.",
    "Ecological and observation uncertainty interacted at the evidence-design level: 51/387 rows had W1O1 burden strictly larger than both W1O0 and W0O1 burdens.",
    "The interaction was especially pervasive for biotic stress: all 43 W1 target-unresolved biotic-stress fibers showed a strict joint burden increment.",
    "Ecological universe expansion created a new need for explicit assay-process calibration in nine rows: two climate, four biotic-stress and three barrier-restoration fibers.",
    "Most strict joint interactions did not require explicit calibration; additional assay channels could instead provide target-level self-calibration.",
    "The complete frozen nine-action library robustly resolved every W1O1 future binary target.",
    "The correct robustness object is therefore a joint-universe evidence profile, not a certificate computed under ecological uncertainty or observation uncertainty in isolation."
  ],
  "claim_boundary": [
    "The systematic assay world remains a synthetic deterministic miscoding fixture.",
    "Strict joint interaction is an exact finite-set burden contrast, not a generic statistical interaction parameter.",
    "Action counts are combinatorial information counts rather than monetary, temporal, logistical or ethical field costs.",
    "The result combines already frozen universes and transformations; it does not establish robustness to undeclared ecological or observation processes.",
    "No generic novelty is claimed for robust design under joint model and measurement uncertainty."
